{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793473462181571001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"short-elderly-cock","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":3},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793469694474807001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4f5e826b-d7c6-49de-80ff-458ea731b0b2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dff5-6fe2-646c-4a0e"},{"link_uuid":"68206cb1-b64b-4b25-8e83-0aa977824177","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e152-4009-4180-4fd8"}],"description":"## Observation\n\nOn 2026-10-28 at 17:47:26 PDT (2026-10-29 00:47:26 UTC) the kernel killed the on-box `rebar-mcp` process for exceeding its container memory limit (bug teenage-unquieted-ringworm; the memory side is fixed in 451212e377a). Docker restarted the container in place (`restart=always`, same port 8092). What followed:\n\n- nginx answered `/mcp/` with 502 from 00:47:27 to at least 00:47:53 UTC (`upstream prematurely closed`, then `connect() failed (111)`, then `recv() failed (104)`). The first non-502 `/mcp` response was at 00:48:14 UTC. The outage lasted 27-47 seconds.\n- Claude Code 2.1.308 (session a85e3cd3, its `mcp-logs-rebar` log) logged 3 \"Terminal connection error\"s, closed the transport, and then made 5 reconnection attempts at 1 s, 2 s, 4 s and 8 s backoff. All 5 got 502, the last at 00:47:43 UTC, 16 s after the kill. It then logged \"Max reconnection attempts (5) reached, giving up\".\n- That session made no further connection attempts. Every rebar tool call it made afterwards failed with \"MCP server 'rebar' has disconnected\": 21 calls between 2026-10-29 00:51 UTC and 2026-10-31 01:03 UTC, while the server was healthy and serving other clients.\n\nSo one server crash leaves every connected Claude Code session disconnected until a human runs `/mcp` reconnect. The client's 16-second retry window is shorter than the container's restart time. An agent in such a session sees an opaque \"disconnected\" error and cannot distinguish it from a server outage.\n\n## What the evidence rules out\n\n- Credentials: the PAT file has been unchanged since 2026-09-14, and an authenticated `initialize` returns 200 on 2026-10-31.\n- Store divergence (topnotch-brazen-slug): the failure is at the transport layer (502 / connection refused), before any store access.\n- Blue-green cutovers: cutovers on 2026-10-30/31 produced no 4xx or 5xx on `/mcp`. The server runs StreamableHTTP without per-session state (`Terminating session: None`).\n\n## Expected\n\nA crash-restart of the MCP container should not outlast a standard client's reconnect window, or the edge should hold or answer requests during the restart instead of returning 502.\n\n## Candidate directions (for planning, not decided)\n\n- Restart into the blue-green standby slot, or keep a warm standby, so nginx fails over (`proxy_next_upstream`) instead of returning 502 while the killed slot restarts.\n- Shorten the time from container start to accepting traffic. On 2026-10-31 it took about 22 s (container start 14:34:37 UTC, cutover 14:34:59 UTC).\n- Document the operator remedy (`/mcp` reconnect) in docs/mcp-client-setup.md.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] After an induced crash of the MCP process on the box, `/mcp` returns no 502 to clients, or recovers within 15 s, measured from the nginx access log.\n- [ ] A Claude Code client connected during the crash is connected again without manual `/mcp` reconnect, shown by its mcp-logs.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","dff5-6fe2-646c-4a0e"],["relates_to","e152-4009-4180-4fd8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["mcp","infra"],"ticket_id":"3f03-06f0-4ac8-40ca","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP container crash-restart outlasts Claude Code's 16 s reconnect window, leaving sessions disconnected until manual /mcp","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["df21b4ac-2b57-433e-8c29-09227744f522","4f5e826b-d7c6-49de-80ff-458ea731b0b2","68206cb1-b64b-4b25-8e83-0aa977824177"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793473462181571001,"uuid":"de4cde68-505f-499b-9c17-e500353c2bec"}